"""What one code point's simple lowercase is.

The other case table in this engine, and the one the fold table cannot answer.
`(?i)` on a literal is settled while the pattern is being compiled, by turning
the literal into the set of everything that folds onto it, and folddata.mojo is
that set. `(?i)` on a backreference is settled while the row is being walked,
by lowering the character the group matched and the character in front of the
cursor and comparing the two, and that is this table.

Upstream uses two different functions for the two and they disagree on real
text. `(?i)ss` matches `s\u017f` because the long s is in the orbit of `s`,
while `(?i)(s)\1` does not match it because the long s lowers to itself.
`(?i)(\u03c3)\1` does not match sigma followed by final sigma for the same
reason. And it goes the other way round for the dotted capital I, which lowers
to a plain `i`, so `(?i)(\u0130)\1` matches `\u0130i`. Document 96.

Only Python is asked, because a backreference is a construct RE2 has not got,
so there is no second engine here to reconcile with and no second table.

The encoding is the fold table's. A run is a low, a high and a delta, the delta
is added to a code point to get its lowercase, and a code point in no run is
its own lowercase, which is every code point but the 1433 that move. One delta
is not a number: `-1073741824` means the run is a stretch laid out as an upper
code point followed by its lower, so an even code point lowers to the one above
it and an odd one lowers to itself. That marker is what turns 668 runs into
214, since without it every letter of such a stretch is a run on its own.

There are 1433 code points whose lowercase is not themselves, covered by 214
runs, 27 of which carry the marker. The other 187 take 81 different deltas
between them, from -42319 to 38864, and 62 of those take the delta of 1 that
the marker itself stands for, left as plain runs because the stretch of pairs
there was too short to be worth marking.

Generated by tools/gen_regexlower.py against CPython 3.13.12 with Unicode
15.1.0, committed rather than built because the Mojo build has no Python in it.
It is the same interpreter folddata.mojo was generated against and the same
skew applies: a later CPython carries a later Unicode and moves a few dozen
code points, so this table is the answer of the version named here rather than
of whichever version happens to be running. The generator checks that walking
these runs reproduces the lowercase of every code point in Unicode, so a
release that moves the answer fails there rather than drifting.
"""

comptime LOWER_RUNS: Int = 214
"""How many runs there are, written out so that a reader of the table does not
have to materialize one of the arrays to ask.
"""

comptime LOWER_EVEN_ONLY: Int32 = -1073741824
"""The delta that means the run alternates upper and lower in pairs.

A code point in a run carrying this one lowers to the code point above it when
it is even and lowers to itself when it is odd. It is a number no real delta
can be, since no lowercase is that far from its code point, and it is the
difference between a couple of hundred runs and most of a thousand.
"""

